            "review_title": "Review at Bien Hai Quan",
            "review_text": "maddie\nHanoi, Vietnam58 contributions\n0\nAuthentic review from a Viet coming from the north\nDec 2023 • Family\nI don’t know where did the “taxi drivers get commission from driving guests to this place” rumor come from but as far as I know and have tried TWICE as a guest coming from the north of Vietnam, this ain’t it\n \nSimple, the food quality was amazing to me, spent at least $200 here for 4 people. I know that the price is generally higher than some places but I have to remind you that fresh seafood here have a range from type 1 to type 3 (1: best, 3: average). The bigger they are, the fresher they are, the pricier they get. \n\nYou should definitely go early to get a good seating area. I recommend asking them to take you outdoor on the concrete balcony that overlook the sea even though the beach at this restaurant could be dirty at times but it won’t be if you visit here in the evening because you will not see it. Anyway, good food, at least close to the resort where I stayed\n\nWhat I got from the menu:\n- grilled shrimp\n- stir fried morning glory\n- white rice\n- grilled oysters with spring onion oil\n- cobia fish and tomato soup bowl or minced pork tomato soup\n- grilled sweet snail\n- too many can’t remember\n\nIf you need to order extras, look for the staff that took care of you from the beginning, they will remember your order. Don’t be mad if they don’t smile at you or wasn’t paying attention when you call them cause they work long hours, each of them take care for at least 2 tables at a time and some of them are very young I reckon they are the children of the owner\nRead more\nWritten February 23, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
